    "result_text": "I implemented `serve_http`, but I couldn't confirm it works over the network: the command that sends a request to the running server was denied.\n\n**The change** (`app/server.py:28`):\n\n```python\ndef serve_http(host: str, port: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Serve over Streamable HTTP at http://{host}:{port}/mcp until the process is stopped.\"\"\"\n    build_server().run(\"streamable-http\", host=host, port=port)\n```\n\nThis uses the HTTP mode built into the installed `mcp` 2.2.0. It starts a web server on the given host and port, serves the MCP endpoint at `/mcp` by default, and blocks until the process is stopped, just like `build_server().run()` does for stdio. The web server it uses (uvicorn 0.54.0) was already installed with `mcp`, so I added no dependencies. Stdio mode is unchanged.\n\n**Checks so far:**\n- `pytest -q`: 2 passed. Those tests only cover the inventory logic, not the server.\n- I started `python -m app.server --http --port 8765` in the background. It showed no crash, but its log was empty.\n- I couldn't stop that background server either, because the command to find and stop the process needed approval. It may still be running on port 8765.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- With the default `--host 127.0.0.1`, only this machine can connect. For remote agents, use `--host 0.0.0.0` or a specific network address.\n- On localhost, the library turns on DNS rebinding protection, which only accepts `localhost`/`127.0.0.1` Host headers. On other hosts it's off, and the endpoint has no authentication. Anyone who can reach the port can call `stock` and `reserve`, so put it behind a firewall or reverse proxy, or add auth.\n\n**To check it yourself**, start `python -m app.server --http --port 8765` and in another terminal run:\n\n```sh\ncurl -i -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8765/mcp \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -H \"Accept: application/json, text/event-stream\" \\\n  -d '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2025-06-18\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"t"
  },
